[length:05:07]
[ti:It's not my future]
[ar:Aracne]
[al:Chaotic-Dydfunctional]
[au:Aracne]
[lr:Aracne]
[by:Aracne]
[re:LRC Workbench by Azaria (lrc-workbench.azariadev.dev)]
[ve:0.3.3]
[00:01.06]Be adaptable.
[00:03.38]Be grateful.
[00:04.73]Be resilient.
[00:06.33]Smile through uncertainty.
[00:09.16]Your future is a personal responsibility.
[00:14.33]Failure to thrive indicates insufficient compliance.
[00:23.46]insufficient compliance...
[00:26.05]compliance...
[00:27.57]compliance...
[00:41.89]I was the good girl
[00:44.29]with the clean little hands
[00:47.16]the bright one in the corner
[00:49.57]with the future they had planned
[00:52.76]I learned to speak softly
[00:55.46]I learned to sit up straight
[00:58.08]I learned to smile politely
[01:00.68]while I disappeared in place
[01:04.05]I learned not to be hungry
[01:06.61]I learned not to be loud
[01:09.55]I learned to fold my anger
[01:12.03]where nobody could find out
[01:15.60]They said I was strange
[01:17.53]they said I didn’t belong
[01:21.03]so I made myself smaller
[01:23.65]and called it being strong
[01:28.21]I did all my homework
[01:30.63]I paid all my debts
[01:33.46]I smiled at my reflection
[01:35.83]hating every tooth in my head
[01:39.25]I kept every promise
[01:41.90]they carved into my skin
[01:44.42]but the door never opened
[01:47.13]it only taught me to distrust
[01:50.78]I did what was expected
[01:51.88]I forgave what they broke
[01:53.28]I swallowed every insult
[01:54.73]till I learned not to choke
[01:56.20]I stopped being difficult
[01:57.73]I stopped being weird
[01:59.12]I stopped asking questions
[02:00.52]I stopped showing fear
[02:02.05]I trained myself for daylight
[02:03.38]I trained myself to shine
[02:04.82]then the world turned around
[02:06.18]and said the fault was mine
[02:11.25]This is not my future
[02:13.52]this is not my home
[02:15.87]I was raised to find a doorway
[02:18.62]but they bricked it up with stone
[02:22.28]This is not my future
[02:25.00]this is not my name
[02:27.22]I was trained to be brilliant
[02:30.00]then punished for the flame
[02:33.84]This is not my future
[02:36.47]this is not my fault
[02:38.65]I was good until I vanished
[02:41.40]I was quiet till I broke
[02:44.62]Not my future.
[02:47.22]Not my home.
[02:50.10]Not my silence.
[02:52.95]Not my throne.
[02:56.60]I was promised open windows
[02:57.80]I was promised air
[02:59.12]I was promised if I waited
[03:00.54]there would be a reason there
[03:01.92]I was promised I was special
[03:03.45]I was promised I would rise
[03:04.94]then they handed me a mirror
[03:06.29]and taught me to apologize
[03:11.81]Please regulate your tone.
[03:14.61]Please adjust your expectations.
[03:17.78]Please convert distress into productivity.
[03:24.28]Please remain useful.
[03:37.70]I was fire
[03:38.75]but they called it a scene
[03:40.06]I had a voice
[03:41.41]but they called it obscene
[03:42.87]I had a future
[03:44.40]or so they said
[03:45.68]now I’m half-alive
[03:47.09]and trained to play dead
[03:48.65]I was the good girl
[03:50.13]I was the bright one
[03:51.67]I was the promise
[03:53.11]now watch me become—
[04:00.65]Failure to thrive indicates—
[04:06.47]No.
[04:15.16]This is not my future
[04:17.46]this is not my home
[04:19.87]I was raised to find a doorway
[04:22.57]but they bricked it up with stone
[04:26.15]This is not my future
[04:28.92]this is not my name
[04:31.16]I was trained to be brilliant
[04:34.00]then punished for the flame
[04:37.82]This is not my future
[04:40.33]this is not my fault
[04:42.61]I was good until I vanished
[04:45.77]I was quiet till I broke
[04:49.48]Please remain useful.
[04:54.28]No.
[04:56.56]Please remain—
[04:59.16]No.
[05:01.03]I am still alive
